---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="About the P4A">
  <main>
    <div class="container pt-18">
      <header class="mb-12">
        <h1 class="text-5xl text-p4a-bg1 font-bold">Meet the the P4A</h1>
        <p class="text-2xl font-semibold">An independent, nonpartisan, and practical civic platform</p>
      </header>

      <section class="mb-10">
        <h2 class="text-3xl text-p4a-bg1 font-bold mb-2">Our Mission</h2>
        <p class="mb-4 leading-relaxed">
          The Playbook for America (P4A) exists to improve how government works by giving people a meaningful voice in shaping democratic ideas and priorities in the United States.
        </p>
        <p class="leading-relaxed">
          Organized as a nonpartisan nonprofit, P4A operates an online platform where citizens and government officials can crowdsource, discuss, and rank ideas and programs, with a focus on turning the most promising ones into actionable solutions. Our aim is to elevate the strongest proposals from all corners of the nation and encourage more people to actively participate in developing solutions that lead to real-world impact and tangible public benefit.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-10">
        <h2 class="text-3xl text-p4a-bg1 font-bold mb-2">Our Vision</h2>
        <p class="leading-relaxed">
          We envision a United States where public policy is informed by the collective intelligence of its people, institutions are effective and trusted, and civic life is inclusive and healthy. In this future, citizens and public servants work together to move ideas from discussion to action—strengthening communities at home and helping the United States play a responsible role addressing global challenges to make the world a better place.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-9">
        <h2 class="text-3xl text-p4a-bg1 font-bold mb-2">Our Values</h2>
        <p class="leading-relaxed">
          P4A is grounded in a commitment to nonpartisanship, openness, and respect for diverse perspectives. We believe the best ideas can come from anywhere, that constructive dialogue is essential to a healthy democracy, and that transparency and fairness are critical to building trust. We value collaboration between citizens and government, and we are guided by a focus on practical, evidence-informed solutions.
        </p>
      </section>


      <section class="mb-10">
        <h2 class="text-3xl text-p4a-bg1 font-bold mb-2">Founders Backstory</h2>
        <p class="mb-4 leading-relaxed">
          I'm <a class="underline text-p4a-bg1 hover:text-p4a-bg2" href="https://linkedin.com/in/jknapp" target="_blank">John Knapp</a>, I build software that helps people improve their lives and communities.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-4 leading-relaxed">
          I believe most Americans want to improve government, strengthen democracy, renew civic life, and help the United States contribute to a better world. The way I see it, far fewer feel invited or equipped to act on those ideas—and when people don't see how their participation can lead to real progress, they disengage.
        <p class="mb-4 leading-relaxed">
          I want P4A to engage and activate those citizens—not only by surfacing and strengthening good ideas, but by inspiring the people who care about them. That includes highlighting opportunities for involvement where their time, expertise, or resources can make a meaningful difference.
        </p>
        <!-- <p class="leading-relaxed">
          I welcome your partcipation.
        </p> -->
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>
